<title>NEW ZEALAND: Foreign share of NZ govt securities 55.5 in Dec.</title>
<headline>Foreign share of NZ govt securities 55.5 in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proportion of New Zealand government securities held by foreigners rose in December to 55.5 percent from 54.8 percent in November, the Reserve Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Survey of non-resident holders:</p>
<p>		    Dec 1996	   Nov  1996	  Dec 1995</p>
<p>		    Value     Pct(*) Value   Pct(*)   Value   Pct(*)</p>
<p>T-bills	     3,510.7  41.1   3,384.1 39.2     4,046.3 56.5</p>
<p>Govt Bonds	 11,375.3  62.2  11,265.4 62.1     7,474.7 39.5</p>
<p>Total Securities 14,886.0  55.5  14,649.5 54.8    11,521.0 44.2</p>
<p>Benchmark Bonds</p>
<p>    07/97	   877.0    44.7     966.6  49.3	581.9  29.6</p>
<p>    07/98	 1,603.9    65.5   1,498.7  61.2	798.2  32.6</p>
<p>    02/00	 1,790.5    59.5   1,838.1  61.0	948.7  31.5</p>
<p>    02/01	 1,515.2    75.8   1,345.8  70.8	192.2  20.8</p>
<p>09/01</p>
<p>    03/02	 1,496.0    59.6   1,350.8  53.8     1,174.1 46.7</p>
<p>    04/04	 1,864.3    61.2   2,084.2  68.5     2,140.2 70.3</p>
<p>    11/06	 2,079.0    74.9   2,040.6  73.5	 771.0 36.7</p>
<p>    02/16	   149.4    34.6     140.6  36.8</p>
<p>(*) percentage's represent non-resident holding as a percent of total securities in market.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
